<summary style="cursor:pointer; padding:16px 18px; background-color:#F7F8FA; font-size:18px; font-weight:600;">
Music Recommendation Systems
</summary>
<div style="padding:18px 24px; background:white; border-top:1px solid #E5E7EB;">
<div style="display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:14px;">
<div style="display:inline-block; font-size:12px; font-weight:700; color:white; background:#2E7D32; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; white-space:nowrap; margin-top:2px;">
Uses AI
</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.45; color:#555;">
Music recommendation systems use AI to analyze listening history and preferences to predict and improve song or artist suggestions.
</div>
</div>
</div>
</details>
</div>
</div>

<!--Smart Home Devices-->
<div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:24px; max-width:1100px; margin:20px auto;">
<iframe src="https://micahkennedy.github.io/embeddings/" width="190" height="70" style="border:none; overflow:hidden; flex-shrink:0; display:block; margin-top:8px;"></iframe>
<div style="flex:1;">
<details style="margin-bottom:12px; border:1px solid #D9DDE3; border-radius:10px; overflow:hidden; background:white;">
<summary style="cursor:pointer; padding:16px 18px; background-color:#F7F8FA; font-size:18px; font-weight:600;">
Smart Home Devices
</summary>
<div style="padding:18px 24px; background:white; border-top:1px solid #E5E7EB;">
<div style="display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:14px;">
<div style="display:inline-block; font-size:12px; font-weight:700; color:white; background:#B56A00; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; white-space:nowrap; margin-top:2px;">
It Depends
</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.45; color:#555;">
<div style="font-style:italic; margin-bottom:6px;">This one’s tricky on purpose.</div>
Some smart home devices follow simple rules, while others use AI to learn routines or recognize voices, so it depends on how they are designed.
</div>
</div>
</div>
</details>
</div>
</div>

<!--Digital Cameras-->
<div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:24px; max-width:1100px; margin:20px auto;">
<iframe src="https://micahkennedy.github.io/embeddings/" width="190" height="70" style="border:none; overflow:hidden; flex-shrink:0; display:block; margin-top:8px;"></iframe>
<div style="flex:1;">
<details style="margin-bottom:12px; border:1px solid #D9DDE3; border-radius:10px; overflow:hidden; background:white;">
<summary style="cursor:pointer; padding:16px 18px; background-color:#F7F8FA; font-size:18px; font-weight:600;">
Digital Cameras
</summary>
<div style="padding:18px 24px; background:white; border-top:1px solid #E5E7EB;">
<div style="display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:14px;">
<div style="display:inline-block; font-size:12px; font-weight:700; color:white; background:#B56A00; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; white-space:nowrap; margin-top:2px;">
It Depends
</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.45; color:#555;">
<div style="font-style:italic; margin-bottom:6px;">This one’s tricky on purpose.</div>
Digital cameras use sensors and electronics to capture images, and while some features such as face-detection may use AI, the main photo-taking process does not.
</div>
</div>
</div>
</details>
</div>
</div>

> **💬 Quick Reflection:** Before you move on, think of a technology you use at school or at home. Classify your example as AI or Not. To help you decide, ask yourself whether the technology:
> - Senses the environment?
> - Learns from data?
> - Makes predictions or decisions?

